  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-tool-antigravity",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-tool-antigravity)\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://github.com/Jaylor-Wang/dsh-tool-antigravity/releases)\n[](tests/)\n[](tsconfig.json)\n\nHigh-performance, streamlined Antigravity capability bundle plugin for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (DSH)."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-tool-antigravity",
      "text": "Provides private Google OAuth 2.0 PKCE authentication, smart multi-account pooling with seamless quota failover, multi-model LLM routing (`google-antigravity`), session-persistent Nano Banana 2 image generation and editing (`generate_image`, `list_images`), and an interactive Web settings panel with live quota visualization.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Highlights in v0.5.3",
      "text": "- **Normalize `anyOf` / `oneOf` Tool Schemas for Claude VALIDATED Mode (Fixes #12 / PR #13)**: Resolved HTTP 400 `PROTOCOL_DRIFT` error on `antigravity-claude-opus-5-5` and `antigravity-claude-sonnet-5-5` when tool definitions contain `anyOf` or `oneOf` unions (such as `generate_image.references.items`, DSH built-in `schedule_*`, `task_board_update`, or MCP tools).\n- **Claude Schema Normalization & Discriminated Union Merging**: Pre-merges multi-branch `object` unions into unified schemas preserving all branch properties and discriminant keys, merges open string presets, and pipelines schemas through `@cortexkit/antigravity-auth-core`'s `toGeminiSchema(..., { claudeValidated: true })`.\n- **Accurate Claude Tool Type Hints**: Lowercases type representations in `claudeToolTypeHint` so `STRICT PARAMETERS:` system instructions emit clean type hints (e.g. `ARRAY_OF_OBJECTS[kind: string REQUIRED, handle: string, path: string]`) without `ARRAY_OF_UNKNOWN`."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. High-Performance Core Architecture",
      "text": "- **TLS Connection Pooling & Session Resumption**: Built-in HTTP/1.1 Keep-Alive socket pool and TLS session resumption against Google endpoints, eliminating repeated TLS handshake roundtrips and significantly reducing Time-To-First-Token (TTFT).\n- **Sliding-Window Buffer SSE Parser**: High-throughput binary chunking directly locates newline separators on raw Buffers, bypassing heavy string concatenations and drastically reducing V8 heap allocations and GC spikes during long reasoning chains.\n- **Granular Thinking Budgets**: Fine-grained reasoning effort configuration (`low`, `medium`, `high`) across Gemini and Claude models with graceful fallbacks.\n- **Pre-flight Idempotent Retry**: Automatically retries transient network interruptions (e.g. TLS RST / 502 / 503 / 504) up to 3 times with exponential backoff prior to first byte emission.\n- **Windows File Lock Recovery**: Active PID probing (`process.kill(pid, 0)`) detects stale locks from crashed processes and immediately frees them, preventing 30-second hang timeouts.\n- **Stale-While-Revalidate (SWR) Quota Resilience**: Robust quota normalization supporting 5h and weekly windows; retains and displays last-known valid quota with smoo"
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Supported Models (`google-antigravity`)",
      "text": "| Model Identifier | Display Name | Capabilities | Thinking Budget |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `antigravity-gemini-4-argon` | Gemini 4 Argon | Text, Vision, Tools | Low / Medium / High |\n| `antigravity-gemini-3.8-flash` | Gemini 3.8 Flash | Text, Vision, Tools | Low / Medium / High |\n| `antigravity-gemini-3.5-flash` | Gemini 3.5 Flash | Text, Vision, Tools | Low / Medium / High |\n| `antigravity-claude-opus-5-5` | Claude Opus 5.5 | Text, Vision, Tools | Low / Medium / High |\n| `antigravity-claude-sonnet-5-5` | Claude Sonnet 5.5 | Text, Vision, Tools | Low / Medium / High |\n| `antigravity-gpt-oss-120b-medium` | GPT-OSS 120B Medium | Text, Vision, Tools | Fixed Effort |"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Nano Banana 2 Image Generation & Multi-Turn Editing",
      "text": "- **`generate_image`**: Prompt-based image creation and iterative image-to-image editing powered by Nano Banana 2 (`gemini-3.1-flash-image`) using session references.\n- **`list_images`**: Inspect and retrieve generated image attachments within the current session.\n- Fully integrated with DSH `AttachmentStore` and `FileSystem` with TOCTOU path escape protection without polluting chat context with raw base64 payloads.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Via DSH Plugin CLI (Recommended)",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Add directly to your active DSH web profile",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-tool-antigravity\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Via npm / pnpm",
      "text": "```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "Using npm",
      "text": "npm install dsh-tool-antigravity"
    },
    {
      "section": "Using pnpm",
      "text": "pnpm add dsh-tool-antigravity\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Cordis Plugin Configuration",
      "text": "Add the plugin entries to your `cordis.patch.yml` or DSH config file:\n\n```yaml\n- id: antigravity-auth\n  name: 'dsh-tool-antigravity'\n\n- id: antigravity-image\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Slash Commands",
      "text": "Manage authentication directly from the DSH terminal / chat prompt:\n\n- `/antigravity-auth login`: Initiates Google OAuth 2.0 PKCE login and launches your default browser.\n- `/antigravity-auth status`: Check current authentication state, masked email, and project id.\n- `/antigravity-auth logout`: Discard credentials and revoke tokens.\n- `/antigravity-auth cancel`: Abort an ongoing login attempt."
    },
    {
      "section": "UI Settings & Dashboard",
      "text": "Once loaded in the DSH Web client:\n- **Antigravity Auth Settings Card**: View live login status, account identifier, and toggle capabilities.\n- **Quota Visualizer**: Real-time remaining quota percentages and countdowns for 5-hour and weekly reset windows.\n- **Image Generation Card**: Configure default image models and batch size.\n\n---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Security & Invariants",
      "text": "1. **Credential Isolation**: Access and refresh tokens are strictly held in host-side secure stores and are never forwarded to the frontend UI, logs, or command done events.\n2. **Strict Loopback Guard**: Account RPC endpoints fail-closed (`loopback-required`) unless the web service is explicitly bound to `127.0.0.1`.\n3. **Immutable Wire Identity**: Emits verified AGY CLI headers (`antigravity/cli/1.1.24`) and attribution metadata.\n4. **Media Path Containment**: All file references are verified against directory traversal and symlink escapes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security & Invariants",
      "text": "---"
    },
    {
      "section": "Disclaimer",
      "text": "This project is an unofficial, community-driven capability bundle intended strictly for personal research, educational purposes, and independent development. Please adhere to relevant platform Terms of Service.\n\n---"
    },
    {
